# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# The licence texts the APK's native Skia library owes on the release
# page, each pinned by SHA-256 (ADR-0057 decisions 3 and 4; the
# component list is apps/human-android/STORE-CHECK.md's "The native Skia
# library", and the template's {freetype_credit} and
# {third_party_notice_texts} are what tools/ci/skia_notices.py fills).
#
# Every source is the component's own file at the commit Skia's DEPS pins
# for rust-skia/skia tag m153-0.101.2, the build skia-binaries.pin names,
# except cpu_features. Its object is in the prebuilt libskia.a, compiled
# by rust-skia's CI from the NDK that CI used, which this pin cannot name;
# this repository's NDK compiles none of it. The text is the licence
# header of NDK 28.2.13676358's copy, read 2026-10-20 as the
# representative one; it is not shown to be the linked copy's. A source is
#   https://...          a file, as fetched
#   gitiles:https://...  a googlesource file, served base64 (?format=TEXT)
#   ndk:<version>/<path> a file of that NDK, under ANDROID_NDK_HOME's
#                        parent or $ANDROID_HOME/ndk; only its first
#                        comment, its licence header, is printed
# The SHA-256 is of the whole file. Renewed with skia-binaries.pin, by
# reading the new DEPS: a changed text fails the run until it is.
#
# component | file | source | sha256
